From 1aafb60b79026c52434df8af3a9332951ba102a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:47:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] batch: background prompt reads in a top-row slot beside
 the groups, paused for every line, finished through the yield pin (opt-in
 STRATA_READS=N)

A BGEN with bg=<park> hands its batched parts (read_plan) to the background at the first batched part: [0, at) is
copied into the park slot (park_yield), the request ends with BREAD <slot> <park> <at>, DONE cancel, BADM 0.  Between
the lines the held reads run one at a time (read_sched order, STRATA_READS_QUANTUM chunks each while others wait) on a
thread of their own with the prefill bound to the park slot's sessions, the groups pumped beside them (the overlap
gate for that slot); any line but BSTOP/BYIELD pauses the run at a chunk boundary that keeps its chunks.  Their
checkpoints (cuts and periodic) come from the stages' parts into the read's own list with the serial rules.  BPP
<park> progress, BREADY <park> <h> once read: the server sends the request again with yslot=<park> and it finishes on
the main sessions and the main verifier (stage 1's pin, cuts from resume0, windows parts, first token).  BSTOP <park>
cancels (BRDONE <park> cancel); a read that cannot go on is dropped (BRDONE <park> err).  Refused beside the groups for
STRATA_READS_GATE_WAIT_MS it reads a quantum with the groups drained.  Region 0 of the M-RoPE table is set back to the
identity between lines when a picture request left it (slot regions only).  Test knobs STRATA_READS_FORCE_BG,
STRATA_READS_TEST_PAUSE_EVERY.  Unset: bg= is ignored, nothing of it runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
